Advanced — protected Trap

Consider:

package a;

public class Parent {
    protected int x;
}

and:

package b;

class Child extends Parent {
    void test(Parent p, Child c) {
        System.out.println(x);
        System.out.println(c.x);
        // System.out.println(p.x);
    }
}

